      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the areas of both the square and the circle and then determine the difference between these areas.\n\n1. **Calculate the side length of the square:**\n   The diagonal of a square with side length \\( s \\) is given by \\( s\\sqrt{2} \\). We know the diagonal is 5 inches, so we can set up the equation:\n   \\[\n   s\\sqrt{2} = 5\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( s \\), we get:\n   \\[\n   s = \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\approx 3.5355\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the area of the square:**\n   The area \\( A_{\\text{square}} \\) of a square is given by \\( s^2 \\):\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{square}} = \\left( \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right)^2 = \\frac{25 \\cdot 2}{4} = \\frac{50}{4} = 12.5 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the radius of the circle:**\n   The diameter of the circle is 5 inches, so the radius \\( r \\) is:\n   \\[\n   r = \\frac{5}{2} = 2.5 \\text{ inches}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the area of the circle:**\n   The area \\( A_{\\text{circle}} \\) of a circle is given by \\( \\pi r^2 \\):\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{circle}} = \\pi (2.5)^2 = \\pi \\cdot 6.25 \\approx 19.634954084936208 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the difference in area between the circle and the square:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area difference} = A_{\\text{circle}} - A_{\\text{square}} \\approx 19.634954084936208 - 12.5 = 7.134954084936208 \\approx 7.1 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the circle is greater than the area of the square by \\(\\boxed{7.1}\\) square inches.",
